<title>ITALY: Italian parliament approves main body of budget.</title>
<headline>Italian parliament approves main body of budget.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The lower house of parliament has approved the main body of the government's 1997 budget, which is designed to cut 62.5 trillion lire off next year's deficit, political sources said.</p>
<p>The so-called connected draft law, which contains all the main cost cutting and revenue raising measures, along with an outline for planned fiscal reform, was passed early on Friday morning at the end of a marathon parliamentary sitting.</p>
</text>
